 stimulation with energy recovery [Dissertation]</article-title><source>Massachusetts Institute of Technology</source><year>2003</year></element-citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-group><fig id="F1" position="float"><label>Fig. (1)</label><caption><p>Biphasic current waveform.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F1"/></fig><fig id="F2" position="float"><label>Fig. (2)</label><caption><p>(<bold>a</bold>) Complete artificial vision restoration system (<bold>b</bold>) Block diagram of the retinal prosthesis.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F2"/></fig><fig id="F3" position="float"><label>Fig. (3)</label><caption><p>Block diagram of neural implant chip (NIC)</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F3"/></fig><fig id="F4" position="float"><label>Fig. (4)</label><caption><p>Schematic diagram of DRR</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F4"/></fig><fig id="F5" position="float"><label>Fig. (5)</label><caption><p>(<bold>a</bold>) Biphasic width controller (BWC), (<bold>b</bold>) Toggle flip flop (TFF).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F5"/></fig><fig id="F6" position="float"><label>Fig. (6)</label><caption><p>(<bold>a</bold>) Current stimulator, (<bold>b</bold>) Regulated cascade current sink (RCCS).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F6"/></fig><fig id="F7" position="float"><label>Fig. (7)</label><caption><p>Simulation and test of current stimulator.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F7"/></fig><fig id="F8" position="float"><label>Fig. (8)</label><caption><p>Structure of a donut probe.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F8"/></fig><fig id="F9" position="float"><label>Fig. (9)</label><caption><p>5x5 array neural stimulator (NS).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F9"/></fig><fig id="F10" position="float"><label>Fig. (10)</label><caption><p>Block diagram of the NICC.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F10"/></fig><fig id="F11" position="float"><label>Fig. (11)</label><caption><p>(<bold>a</bold>) State diagram of the controller NICC (<bold>b</bold>) status of control signals at different states.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F11"/></fig><fig id="F12" position="float"><label>Fig. (12)</label><caption><p>Schematic diagram of power-on reset.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F12"/></fig><fig id="F13" position="float"><label>Fig. (13)</label><caption><p>Test of POR. 5V is applied all of a sudden and monitored the reset. Trace 1 is the transient voltage rise and Trace 2 is the reset.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F13"/></fig><fig id="F14" position="float"><label>Fig. (14)</label><caption><p>Microscopic view of the test module of 5x5 array NIC.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F14"/></fig><fig id="F15" position="float"><label>Fig. (15)</label><caption><p>Test setup of NIC. Microcontroller (PIC) is programmed with the data of letter &#x0201c;L&#x0201d; as shown in the table on left of the figure. PIC sends this data to the NIC continuously to stimulate the neurons.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F15"/></fig><fig id="F16" position="float"><label>Fig. (16)</label><caption><p>Biphasic pulse width control test. Widths generated by configuration word (<bold>a</bold>) 0x033DF3 (<bold>b</bold>) 0x033DFB (<bold>c</bold>) 0x03BEFF (<bold>d</bold>) 0x03FEFB (<bold>e</bold>) 0x03BFFB.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F16"/></fig><fig id="F17" position="float"><label>Fig. (17)</label><caption><p>Variable data loaded (<bold>a</bold>) P21 = 0x20, P22 = 0x80 (<bold>b</bold>) P52 = 0x20, P53 = 0x80. Measured amplitudes are 0.8V and 3.2V respectively.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F17"/></fig><fig id="F18" position="float"><label>Fig. (18)</label><caption><p>Data loaded is 0x40 in each channel. Measured amplitude is 1.6V.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_F18"/></fig><table-wrap id="T1" position="float"><label>Table 1.</label><caption><p>Specifications of Donut Probe and Probe Array for 20&#x000b5;m Penetration</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" width="100%"><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Parameters/Dimensions</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Penetration</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">20&#x000b5;m</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Stimulating current</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">15.8&#x000b5;A</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Radius of central electrode (r)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">15&#x000b5;m</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Spacing bet. central &#x00026; donut electrodes</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">20&#x000b5;m</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Inner radius of donut electrode (r<sub>1</sub>)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">35&#x000b5;m</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Outer radius of donut electrode (r<sub>2</sub>)</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">38&#x000b5;m</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Thickness of electrodes</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2&#x000b5;m</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Mini. spacing between two probes</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">150&#x000b5;m</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Resolution</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">150&#x000b5;m&#x000d7;150&#x000b5;m</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Material</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">IrO<sub>x</sub></td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2.</label><caption><p>Protocol of Data Transmission</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" width="100%"><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><graphic xlink:href="TOOPHTJ-2-77_FT2"/></td></tr></table></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3.</label><caption><p>NIC&#x02019;s Specifications and Performance for 13.889 KHz Clock</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" width="100%"><thead><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Parameters</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Specification/performance</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Technology<break/>Die size<break/>Probe type<break/>Number of probes<break/>Resolution of probes<break/>Total area of probes<break/>Number of current stimulator<break/>Current Stimulator<break/>Supply voltage<break/>Resolution of current stimulator<break/>Current stimulator output(for input 0-BE)<break/>Current stimulator output(for max. input FF)<break/>Type of waveform(software configurable)<break/><break/><break/><break/>Pulse width(programmable by 6-bit counter)<break/>Data rate<break/>Frame rate<break/>Power consumption (no load)<break/><break/><break/>Power consumption (full load)</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">CMOS 0.5mm<break/>3mm&#x000d7;3mm<break/>Donut probe<break/>5&#x000d7;5 array (25 probes)<break/>150&#x000b5;m&#x000d7;150&#x000b5;m<break/>750&#x000b5;m&#x000d7;750&#x000b5;m<break/>5<break/>8 bits<break/>5V (or 3V)<break/>2.5&#x000b5;A<break/>0-400&#x000b5;A<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="T3FN1">&#x02020;</xref>(Linear range)<break/>430&#x000b5;A<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="T3FN1">&#x02020;</xref>(max.)<break/>Monophasic (anodic)<break/>Monophasic (cathodic)<break/>Biphasic(with interphase delay)<break/>Biphasic(without interphase delay)<break/>0-2.88 ms<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="T3FN2">&#x02021;</xref><break/>13.889 Kbits/sec<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="T3FN2">&#x02021;</xref><break/>55.94 frames/sec<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="T3FN2">&#x02021;</xref><break/>1.59 mW at 3V<break/>13.70 mW at 5V<break/>2.44 mW at 3V<break/>18.65 mW at 5V</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="T3FN1"><label>&#x02020;</label><p>For 5V supply.</p></fn><fn id="T3FN2"><label>&#x02021;</label><p>For clock frequency 13.889KHz</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>